% NY N362002 (June 2026): a plastic foam pad from China.
scenario ny_n362002 is:
    the reticulated foam pad is a manufactured article,
        as stated in ruling NY N362002 at "It is a single piece of die-cut open-cell reticulated polyurethane foam that is circular in shape and intended to suppress splashing".
    the reticulated foam pad is made of plastics,
        as stated in ruling NY N362002 at "As this foam component would be considered an article of plastic".
    the principal use of the reticulated foam pad is splash suppression in an oil drain container,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N362002 at "circular in shape and intended to suppress splashing and agitation of used motor oil as it is drained from a vehicle",
        because "a component permanently incorporated in an oil drain container to suppress splashing; not a filter".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the reticulated foam pad is 3926.90"].

% NY N363254 (July 2026): a plastic rake from China.
scenario ny_n363254 is:
    the Leafinator is a manufactured article,
        as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "It is a garden rake used in household yards".
    the Leafinator is a composite good,
        as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "The item is considered a composite good within the meaning of General Rule of Interpretation (GRI) 3".
    the polypropylene panels of the Leafinator is a component of the Leafinator,
        as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "The rake consists of polypropylene plastic upper and lower scoop panels".
    the aluminium pole of the Leafinator is a component of the Leafinator,
        as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "an aluminum handle and aluminum pole".
    the polypropylene panels of the Leafinator is made of plastics,
        as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "The item consists of a polypropylene (PP) upper rake panel, a polypropylene plastic lower scoop panel".
    the essential character of the Leafinator is given by the polypropylene panels of the Leafinator,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "polypropylene plastic components provides the essential character within the meaning of GRI 3(b)",
        because "the polypropylene components make up most of the weight and bulk and perform the principal function of raking".
    the principal use of the Leafinator is household use,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N363254 at "It is a garden rake used in household yards",
        because "a garden rake used in household yards".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the Leafinator is 3924.90"].

