    the pom pom balls of the Pom Pom Launcher is a component of the Pom Pom Launcher,
        as stated in ruling NY N360066 at "launcher shaped like a gun and fifty pom pom balls".
    the launcher of the Pom Pom Launcher is made of plastics,
        as stated in ruling NY N360066 at "the plastic pom pom launcher is considered a plastic pet toy used by cats and will be classified under heading 3924 as".
    the essential character of the Pom Pom Launcher is given by the launcher of the Pom Pom Launcher,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N360066 at "or component which gives them their essential character which may be determined by the nature of the material or component",
        because "the launcher gives the essential character by bulk, weight, value and importance to the set".
    the principal use of the Pom Pom Launcher is household use,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N360066 at "plastic pet supplies used by domestic household animals are classified as household articles",
        because "plastic pet toys used by domestic animals are household articles (Hartz Mountain Corp. v. United States, 19 CIT 1149)".
    the Pom Pom Launcher is claimed to belong to toys of heading 9503,
        as stated in ruling NY N360066 at "you suggest classification in heading 9503".
    the claim that the Pom Pom Launcher belongs to toys of heading 9503 is rejected,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N360066 at "are identifiable as intended exclusively for animals",
        because "Chapter 95 note 5: heading 9503 does not cover articles identifiable as intended exclusively for animals".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the Pom Pom Launcher is 3924.90"].

