    the WPP BOPP bag is a manufactured article,
        as stated in ruling NY N342911 at "(i) the good is a good wholly obtained or produced entirely in the territory of one or more of the parties to the Agreement".
    the WPP BOPP bag is made of plastics,
        as stated in ruling NY N342911 at "strips 2 mm wide and laminated with plastic visible to the naked eye and classified in heading 5903.".
    the WPP BOPP bag is shaped as sack,
        as stated in ruling NY N342911 at "on the status of WPP/BOPP bags from Dominican Republic-Central America under the DR-CAFTA".
    the WPP BOPP bag contains 100 percent of polypropylene,
        as stated in ruling NY N342911 at "described as a bag made from woven polypropylene (WPP) that is coated on the exterior with melted polypropylene laminated".
    the principal use of the WPP BOPP bag is packing of goods,
        according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N342911 at "The bags are used for packaging products including animal feed",
        because "bags used for packaging animal feed, cat litter, home and garden products and charcoal".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the WPP BOPP bag is 3923.29"].
